From: ProAudio Player <noreply@proaudio-player.local>
Date: Thu, 11 Sep 2026 20:40:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] librespot-discovery: terminate discovery on short credential blob

Spotify Android can occasionally send an empty addUser blob after a stale
zeroconf handshake. librespot 0.8.0 returns HmacError in that case, but the
HTTP request task then panics while the discovery server and spotifyd process
stay alive. Subsequent attempts keep using the stale server key and fail until
spotifyd is restarted.

Discovery already has a ServerError event whose documented behavior is to
terminate the credential stream. Emit that event before returning the existing
error. spotifyd then leaves its broken discovery session and systemd starts a
fresh receiver with a new key instead of remaining discoverable but unusable.

This is deliberately limited to the existing malformed-blob guard and does
not change credential validation or accept invalid Spotify data.
---
 VENDOR/librespot-discovery/src/server.rs | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/VENDOR/librespot-discovery/src/server.rs b/VENDOR/librespot-discovery/src/server.rs
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/VENDOR/librespot-discovery/src/server.rs
+++ b/VENDOR/librespot-discovery/src/server.rs
@@ -131,7 +131,11 @@ impl RequestHandler {
 
         let encrypted_blob_len = encrypted_blob.len();
         if encrypted_blob_len < 16 {
-            return Err(DiscoveryError::HmacError(encrypted_blob.to_vec()).into());
+            let blob = encrypted_blob.to_vec();
+            let _ = self.event_tx.send(DiscoveryEvent::ServerError(
+                DiscoveryError::HmacError(blob.clone()),
+            ));
+            return Err(DiscoveryError::HmacError(blob).into());
         }
 
         let iv = &encrypted_blob[0..16];
-- 
2.51.0
